WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:02.840
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.300
- There's no place like home.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.127
And that's why we're
celebrating as many hometowns

00:00:08.127 --> 00:00:12.100
as we can, all across the
country, all season long.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.720
Next up is Portland, Oregon,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.440
where culinary professional
Judiaann Woo calls home.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.070
I hear she makes it her mission

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.620
to know all the best
restaurants and chefs in town.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.430
Now that's a woman after my own heart.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:26.263
Let's watch.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.593
- Hey, Drew.

00:00:28.593 --> 00:00:31.090
It is Kara Mack, host
of K2's Afternoon Live,

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.120
your sibling show in Portland, Oregon.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.630
And I know you are
celebrating hometown spirit.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.760
Well, no one has more hometown spirit

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.880
than our very own Judiaann Woo.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.450
Judiaann, share with people
why Portland's so awesome.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.700
- [Judiaann] Portland is my
hometown and I love it so much.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.210
There are so many amazing
places to eat and drink,

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.720
plus scenic beauty,
and the most passionate

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.510
and creative people you will ever meet.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.130
- And you're gonna show
it off for everyone.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.653
So we're gonna send you off.

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:55.486
Have so much fun.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.130
- Welcome to OMSI.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:01.670
OMSI stands for the Oregon
Museum of Science and Industry.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.210
It's got something for everybody.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.050
You learn about the earth, the universe,

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.660
and everything in between.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.090
We have here giant
Australian walking sticks.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.110
This is one corner of the museum

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.010
where they have actual live creatures

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.880
that you can interact with such as these.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.253
Say hello to Drew.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.950
I'm here at Toki Restaurant

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.750
in the heart of downtown Portland.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.780
And behind me is Chef Owner, Peter Cho.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.210
He's doing his take on the most delicious,

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:32.060
crave worthy Korean-American classics.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:33.960
This is like, you know, portable food.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.990
So good.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:37.823
- Yes.

00:01:37.823 --> 00:01:39.950
- Well, Drew, that was just
a quick peek at Portland,

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.830
the city we love so much.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.790
We can't wait for you to come visit.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.633
See you soon.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:46.963
- Hey, Drew.

00:01:46.963 --> 00:01:48.010
My name is Tatiana Inise.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:50.110
I'm the elementary
school teacher right here

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.290
in Washington, DC.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.720
Now, DC has my home for
the past couple of years,

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:54.577
and I love it here.

00:01:54.577 --> 00:01:57.300
One of the things that I love
about DC is it's rich history

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.133
and culture.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.720
Now, we're about to go
check out Union Market.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.164
It's my favorite place to
hit up right after work,

00:02:02.164 --> 00:02:03.164
so let's go.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.270
My first stop when I come to Union Market

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.540
is I always go to Puddin'.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.330
Puddin' is a New Orleans
Southern comfort food

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.530
all wrapped into one.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.750
Honestly, the bread pudding is delicious,

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.360
but everything on the menu is delicious.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.000
I normally order the shrimp
and grits or the etouffee.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.750
So if you're Union
Market, check out Puddin'.

00:02:24.318 --> 00:02:26.080
We're here at Meridian Hill Park.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.910
But some locals actually
call it Malcolm X.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.170
Little known fact, I didn't even know

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.290
it was called Meridian Hill park.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.200
I've always referred to as Malcolm X park.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.030
Now on Sundays, they have a drum circle

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.750
and it's absolutely beautiful.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.850
Like live music on a Sunday.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:39.683
Why not?

00:02:39.683 --> 00:02:41.610
It's my favorite place to come
when I just wanna chill out,

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.990
wanna walk my dog, go for a run.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.190
It's just the peace in
the middle of a city.

00:02:48.413 --> 00:02:49.246
All right, Drew.

00:02:49.246 --> 00:02:50.079
That's just a little snapshot
of the Washington DC.

00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:51.810
I hope you love it as much as I do.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.470
Listen, next time you're in town.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.490
Hit me up, girl.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:55.390
I'll see you soon.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.280
- Howdy Drew, I'm Pam
Minick here at KTVT CBS 11

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.320
in Fort Worth Dallas, Texas, along

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.250
with Chief Meteorologist Scott Padgett

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.670
and what we love about
this area of North Texas,

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.630
it's the perfect blend of
cowboys, cowgirl culture,

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.770
and entertainment.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.330
Now we're headed to see
the Dallas Cowboys because.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:16.233
- CBS 11 is your Official Cowboy Station.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.080
- We're at the home of the Cowboys,

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.270
Dallas Cowboys Football Team, that is,

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.730
and my favorite part of the team

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.890
are the Dallas Cowboy Cheerleaders,

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.170
who have a message for you Drew.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.403
- [Cheerleaders] Welcome
to AT and T Stadium.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.480
- How about those moves, Drew?

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.500
You know, even when it's
not football season,

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.840
you've got to see the Cowboy's Stadium,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.420
the size, the scope of it,
the artwork, the memorabilia.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.403
It's worth seeing.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.170
This is the National Cowgirl
Museum and Hall of Fame

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.790
in Fort Worth, Texas where
women who shaped the west

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.080
with their can do spirit are recognized.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.400
And I'm proud to be one of those honorees.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.580
Dr. Diana Vela, what makes
The Cowgirl Museum a must see?

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.730
- We are the only
institution in the nation

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:03.960
that honors those women
who are shaping the west

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.150
and changing the world.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.780
Where else can you see
Miranda Lambert's guitar,

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.970
a Game of Thrones saddle,
and Annie Oakley's shotgun

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.120
in one place?

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.990
- Well, Drew, that's just a little taste

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.430
of what makes Fort
Worth Dallas so special.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.310
I hope you love it as much as I do.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.010
And I can't wait for you to visit.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.190
You know, they say that
everything is bigger in Texas

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:25.473
so I can't wait to show you more.

00:04:26.864 --> 00:04:31.447
("The Drew Barrymore Show Theme Song")

